    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "With the exception of certain intrinsic attributes, which are read-only, any AsciiDoc document attribute (herein "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "attributes"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") may be defined from the CLI, in the playbook, in the component descriptor, or in the header of a page using an attribute entry. The precedence matches that order (higher to lower) unless the precedence has been altered for a given attribute using a modifier. These different scopes give you the ability to define attributes at the level of granularity you need and to be able to override their values for different environments or situations."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This page explains how to define and modify an attribute at the page level using an attribute entry. Alternately, these attributes can be set at a higher level using the CLI, playbook, or component descriptor. The result of defining or modifying an attribute is the same (meaning the processor doesn’t care how it’s defined)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "attribute entry"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is the primary mechanism for defining an attribute for a page and, if applicable, assigning a value to it. You can think of an attribute entry like a global variable assignment in AsciiDoc."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An attribute entry consists of two parts: a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "name"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "value"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Each attribute entry must be entered on its own line in a page header. An attribute entry starts with an opening colon ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "), directly followed by the attribute’s name, and then a closing colon ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). This activates, or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "sets"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", the attribute so you can use it in your page."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Page Title\n:name-of-an-attribute: "
              },
              {
                "guard": null,
                "icons": null,
                "id": "CO1-1",
                "kind": "callout",
                "number": "1",
                "src": "",
                "xml": false
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "colist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "coids": [
                  "CO1-1"
                ],
                "icons": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The attribute’s name is directly preceded with a opening colon ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ") and directly followed by a closing colon ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ")."
                  }
                ],
                "src": ""
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": "arabic",
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In many cases, you explicitly assign a value to an attribute by entering information after its name in the attribute entry. The value must be offset from the closing colon ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") by at least one space."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Page Title\n:name-of-an-attribute: value of the attribute "
              },
              {
                "guard": null,
                "icons": null,
                "id": "CO2-1",
                "kind": "callout",
                "number": "1",
                "src": "",
                "xml": false
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "colist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "coids": [
                  "CO2-1"
                ],
                "icons": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "An explicitly assigned value is offset from the closing colon ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ") by at least one blank space. At the end of the value, press "
                  },
                  {
                    "keys": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Enter"
                        }
